{
  "_comment": [
    "Reference intervals for common laboratory and vital-sign observations,",
    "keyed by LOINC code.",
    "",
    "These are CONVENTIONAL ADULT INTERVALS. Real reference ranges are",
    "established per laboratory, per analyser and per method, and a real report",
    "carries the issuing laboratory's own. Nothing here is authoritative for",
    "interpreting a real result.",
    "",
    "They exist so a generated Observation carries the range its value was meant",
    "to be compared against — which is what a downstream consumer needs in order",
    "to render a report, or to score whether a system spotted an abnormal result,",
    "without having to invent a range whose guess would not match the one the",
    "module author had in mind.",
    "",
    "A code maps to a list of variants, tried in order; the first whose selectors",
    "match the patient wins. Selectors: 'sex' (M/F) and 'min_age' in years. A",
    "variant with no selectors matches anyone, so it belongs last.",
    "",
    "Codes absent from this file get no referenceRange and no interpretation,",
    "which is the previous behaviour."
  ],

